WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.768
-Our first guest tonight
is a Grammy-nominated singer,

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:03.970
songwriter, actress,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.172
and one of the biggest
superstars on the planet.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.841
She recently released
her first live album,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.644
"Attention: Miley Live."
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.479
our friend Miley Cyrus,
everybody.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:15.881
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:18.885
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:23.990
♪♪

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:29.062
♪♪

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.330
Welcome back!
-Thank you.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.099
-So happy to have you here.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.868
Hello, everyone.
Good to see you.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.303
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.006
-This is -- This is very --
A live album is very exciting.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.141
And there you go, right here.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.876
-And I would imagine one of
the coolest things about it

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.545
is picking the songs.
-Yes.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.746
-And I'm wondering,
are they the songs

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.249
you most like to sing
or the ones you feel like

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.817
your fans most like to hear?

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.052
-I let my fans
create this set list,

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.721
because it's been two years

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.090
since we've celebrated
live music together.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.258
To be honest,
I'm still getting used to

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.360
coming out of this cocoon
that we've all been in

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.129
for the last couple of years.
I think a lot of us

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.032
have been struggling
with anxiety and fear

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.134
and socially
just getting used to

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.469
connecting with each other
again.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:10.803
So I thought it would bring
some hope and joy

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.538
and also just make me feel
more comfortable

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:15.474
knowing that my fans are happy
and knowing that I'm able

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.210
to express to them
how much I've missed them

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.178
over the last two years.
-I think that's the way

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.280
a lot of live performers I know
felt.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.815
Did you have anxiety
about going back onstage

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.183
for the first time after?
-Yes.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.919
I have anxiety right now,
to be honest with everyone.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.220
-Well, we're gonna
get through that.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.722
-You know?
And I think a lot of us

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.158
have been struggling with that,
just because integrating

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.260
into a world
that felt very familiar

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.930
but now feels new.
I'm really excited,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.398
'cause Happy Hippie,
my foundation,

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:41.134
has partnered
with my longtime therapist

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.569
for Change Your Brain,
Change Your Life,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.571
trying to help with everybody,
get used to this new normal

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.506
and seeing everyone
with masks on.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.675
And it's hard to see
my fans sing along,

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.077
because a lot of them
are wearing masks,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.979
so I can't tell if they
hate it or hate me.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.415
I think you guys hate me,
or I can't tell.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.550
-No, I don't think they do.
-Alright.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.853
They're smiling under there.
Alright.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.254
-You mentioned Happy Hippie.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.755
This has been
quite a few years now

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.057
that you've had this foundation.
-Yes.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.625
-And what was --
In the beginning,

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:10.430
what was it that you were seeing
that most needed attention?

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.565
-I've felt so fortunate
in my life.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.567
I've had parents
that really support me

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.769
in all my decisions
and all my evolutions.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.272
And I've really been
experimental

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:22.074
when it comes to my identity,
my sexuality.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.643
And I really feel
that I've had

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.078
a family that's been
really supportive,

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.980
and I know that that isn't
the case for everyone.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.816
And so I wanted to kind of
just fight that injustice.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.818
And I think everyone
deserves the freedom

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.387
to express themselves
and no matter how they identify.

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:37.156
So that's very important
because again,

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:41.660
everything, I think, comes
from a place of authenticity

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.497
to myself first,
because it's hard to relate

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.100
if you don't feel you identify
with that same struggle.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.735
So even though I've had
a different experience,

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.736
I identify with that.
-Well, that's great.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.338
And it's really sweet that
you're doing that for people.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.508
-I love it. It fulfills me.
-Feeling heard is, I think,

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.444
the most important thing for
kids who are going through that.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.412
-Just letting people know
that you care

00:03:00.412 --> 00:03:02.916
and that you support them.
And I think that's, again,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.283
with the "Attention" live album,

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.684
that's one thing
that I just wanted to do,

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:08.388
is really let my fans know

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.324
how appreciative I am
of their loyalty.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:15.561
They are the only reason
why I live the life that I live,

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:16.962
and I know that.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:19.031
There's not one time
that I get into my bed at night

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.666
or drive myself to work
in my car

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.301
that I don't think about,

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:26.039
my purpose comes
so much from my fans.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.640
And I think we share
that same bond.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.376
I think a lot of what I'm doing
inspires them;

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.412
what they're doing inspires me;
and it's just amazing.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:36.148
-That's great.
You did a great --

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.817
For your fans
and for maybe people

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.085
who already were familiar
with you,

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.753
you had a great NBC
live New Year's Eve special

00:03:41.753 --> 00:03:43.088
last year.
You just announced today

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:44.323
you're going to do it next year.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.758
-You did it with Pete Davidson.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:49.261
-You and Pete had a lovely time
together, it seemed.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:50.463
-Yeah. You know, I'm a very --

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.332
I'm kind of a "go with the flow"
kind of person.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:55.768
But, this, now it seems like
I kind of know what I'm doing

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.670
on New Year's forever.
-That's really nice!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.206
-Which I like.
Because I need boundaries.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:02.274
Someone told me one time,
it's not about

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.377
just having boundaries,
it's about just having bumpers.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.745
Just when you start to veer,

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.013
that you have something
to bounce off of it.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:10.382
So I know that I have to
keep my act together enough

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:12.351
to make it to New Year's.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:15.321
-And that NBC will actually
allow me to be on television

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.423
because there was a couple years
there where it was dicey.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.258
-Yeah.
-Live TV.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.694
I wasn't asked to do
a lot of live TV.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.896
[ Laughter ]
-That's true.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.865
You -- But I will say --
-You let me on here.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.534
-You had -- Yeah, I mean,
you had "SNL."

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.637
You did some "SNL."
-"SNL" is a free-for-all,

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.538
which is why
me and Lorne Michaels...

00:04:33.538 --> 00:04:35.508
Lorne has been my hero

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:38.377
since the first time I did "SNL"
when I was 18.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.113
-Yeah.
-I'm gonna be 30

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.813
by the time
we're doing New Year's.

00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:44.516
So I've been working with him
for the last 12 years,

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:47.419
and I feel like I've had
this really --

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.955
I don't know if anyone's
gotten to have the experience

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.825
that I'm having
of taking Producing 101

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.560
from literally
the greatest of all time.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.894
-Yeah, he knows what he's doing.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:58.498
And you're somebody he would be
drawn to naturally,

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.098
because you are --
-I'll do anything,

00:05:00.098 --> 00:05:01.767
and I'll make an ass of myself.
-There you go.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.968
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.737
-I was gonna say
you're talented.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.139
-Thank you.
-You're professional.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:10.743
But you also --
you present to an audience,

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.512
which I think especially
he likes on "SNL."

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.947
There's some danger to you,
and yet it's not --

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.950
but you're not dangerous the way
you prepare for your art.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.351
-No.
-And so that's the thing

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.287
that he doesn't care for.
But I think

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.821
if you can give that energy out,
which I feel like

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:24.490
you do such a nice job with.
-I think you have to.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.726
If you're gonna do
a show like "SNL,"

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:30.262
if you're going to perform live,
by having structure,

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:32.831
you actually give yourself
an environment to play in,

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:36.235
because without setting that
environment of a safe place,

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.870
it actually gives you
this more --

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:41.307
I guess, more confidence
to be able to improv.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:44.444
I mean, Pete, also, if we're
talking about unreliable,

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:46.245
I didn't know really
what was gonna happen.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.747
He kept joking
about not showing up.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:49.982
But, you know, like,
truth to every joke,

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.216
that's what makes it funny.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:53.552
-So I got very nervous
by, like, the 15th time

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.488
he joked about
not actually showing up.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:58.157
But he showed up, and
he did an incredible job.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:01.561
And the professionalism between
Lorne, Pete, our crew, and

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.896
our guests is the only reason
why we had a New Year show,

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:06.899
because we were really
fighting against COVID.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.967
And at that point,
it was when we were having

00:06:08.967 --> 00:06:10.469
a big surge
towards the end of the year.

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:13.005
And we also wanted to make sure
it was the right thing to do,

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.607
to continue to have the show.
So we did what we could,

00:06:15.607 --> 00:06:18.744
which was, you know,
a very minimal audience.

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.479
We had, at first, said,
you know,

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.149
10,000 of my closest friends.
I barely have 10 friends.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:27.352
But we were gonna cast 10,000
very cool-looking "Miley people"

00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:29.354
that would look like
I had cool friends.

00:06:29.354 --> 00:06:31.357
And then we end up having

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:33.025
actually just
my real friends there,

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:35.328
between me and Pete
and my family.

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:36.796
And we did everything
that we could

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:39.331
to make sure everybody was safe,
but they could still celebrate.

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:41.867
'Cause it felt like,
at the end of that year,

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:43.435
it was something
that everyone really needed.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.037
It's something
that happens every year.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.906
And to break that tradition,
I think,

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.207
could have caused
even more of a panic.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.076
So we did it
as safely as possible.

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:53.145
-You've got a little bit less,
I guess, than seven months.

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.047
Do you start thinking
about next year now,

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.816
or this coming year?
-I just started

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.951
the conversation,
and it started, you know,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:02.321
with all the great advice
that he's been given from,

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.623
whether it's Paul McCartney
or Paul Simon.

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:06.892
Lorne knows more Pauls
than anyone I've ever known.

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:08.860
-He knows all the best Pauls.
-He knows all the best Pauls.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.062
-Do you have a Lorne?

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:11.330
Do you do
a Lorne impression yet?

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:15.701
-I-I don't know
if I do my impression so much

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.771
as more like he's just always
kind of looking at me like this,

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:20.773
but I know I'm gonna do
whatever he says anyway.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.141
-Yeah.
-Like, he's looking like,

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.243
"Yeah, Miley, that's
definitely gonna happen."

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.245
But then I know someone's
gonna call me

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.080
and go, "Lorne doesn't think
it's the best idea."

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.448
-Oh, okay.
-Yeah.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.016
-I have more questions for you.
Mind sticking around?

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:32.351
-For sure.
-We'll be right back

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.053
with more from Miley Cyrus,
everybody.

